                   milliseconds, bytes, disc_number, track_number)
SELECT st.title,
       al.album_id,
       g.genre_id,
       coalesce(c.name, regexp_replace(st.composer, '^DP, ', 'Thomas Bangalter, Guy-Manuel de Homem-Christo, ')),
       d.ms,
       d.ms * 32,
       st.disc,
       st.num
FROM seed_track st
JOIN seed_album sa         ON sa.code = st.album
JOIN artist ar             ON ar.name = sa.artist
JOIN album al              ON al.artist_id = ar.artist_id AND al.title = sa.title
JOIN genre g               ON g.name = coalesce(st.genre, sa.genre)
LEFT JOIN seed_composer c  ON c.code = st.composer
CROSS JOIN LATERAL (
    SELECT (split_part(st.duration, ':', 1)::int * 60
          + split_part(st.duration, ':', 2)::int) * 1000 AS ms
) d
ORDER BY al.album_id, st.disc, st.num;


/*******************************************************************************
   3. Spotify catalog
   Every track in oscargm's Spotify export (Liked Songs, the 20 playlists and
   a year of listening history), with its album and artists.

   The export only has names and Spotify IDs, so each track was looked up on
   Deezer's public API, which gave the album, disc and track number, duration,
   ISRC, release date, label, UPC, cover, artist picture and genres. Tracks
   Deezer doesn't have come from their public Spotify page (duration, track
   number, album, release date). The lists below were generated by a one-off
   script; fix a row here rather than regenerating.

   - Tracks by the featured artists that are on a featured album point to
     those tracks instead of being added again (matched by title, ignoring
     labels such as "- Remastered 2009"; live versions stay separate).
   - Saved albums have every track; other albums only the tracks in the export.
   - Artist names are spelled as in Spotify (PXNDX, not Deezer's "Panda").
   - artist_type is only known for "Various Artists" (various), and composer
     for nobody: neither source has songwriters.
   - bytes is estimated like the featured artists' (milliseconds * 32).
   - 4 tracks that only appear in the listening history couldn't be found and
     are left out.
********************************************************************************/
-- Artists, in name order. Artists of the featured section are reused by name.

